          "value": "\n<ol><li dir=\"ltr\">[...] A.M. , in Jerusalem, the [holy] city [...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] our master and lord Samuel ha-Kohen, \u27e6Head\u27e7 Gaon [...]</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[And I will ...] you, in the manner of Jewish men, who nourish and [...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[And she accepted ... on the conditio]n that she will serve (\"stand before\") him, attend [him ...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... Judah b. A]mram (whose) s(oul is at) r(est) [fixed] for Sutayt, the virgin, the bride [... and ... remain]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...]a strong, firm [d]ebt. And with this understanding [...]</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[... tw]o witnesses on her words. And [this] girl [is of age ...]\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] two broad ... and a zayla\u02bf necklace\u2014twenty [...]</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...] and two mats and three cloa[ks ...]\u00a0\u00a0</li>\n<li dir=\"ltr\">[...]\u2014ten dinars, a festive robe ...\u00a0 </li></ol>\n",
